## arm 1 · wake, a registry exid outside its grammar
✋ ConstraintError: the registry's exid holds a byte outside its grammar
   allowed: [A-Za-z0-9._-]
   ⇒ this value is written into ~/.ssh/config, and a newline there
     adds a directive — ProxyCommand runs a command on THIS box
   fix: rhx git.grove.set grove-fixture-hetzner-grammar --at <user>@<host>:<port>   (an ec2 tunnel's host is localhost; a tailnet grove's is its own name)

## arm 1 · wake, a registry sshAlias whose first byte is '-'
✋ ConstraintError: the registry's sshAlias starts with '-'
   ⇒ it reaches ssh as a positional, and ssh reads a '-' at the front
     as an OPTION — one of them, -oProxyCommand=, runs a command here
   fix: rhx git.grove.set grove-fixture-hetzner-dash --at <user>@<host>:<port>   (an ec2 tunnel's host is localhost; a tailnet grove's is its own name)

## arm 1 · wake, a registry host whose first byte is '-'
✋ ConstraintError: the registry's host starts with '-' — ssh would read it as an option
   fix: rhx git.grove.set grove-fixture-hetzner-hostdash --at <user>@<host>:<port>

