## arm 2 · trust.gen, an unreported key (refused)
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-hetzner --mode apply --trust verified
   ├─ alias:    grove-fixture-hetzner
   ├─ endpoint: grove-fixture-hetzner-1:22
   ├─ tailnet:  no local tunnel — scan grove-fixture-hetzner-1 direct
   ├─ scanned:  2 key(s) offered
   ├─ attest:   the box itself, over ssh pinned to its trusted key (ssh-ed25519)
   ├─ fingerprints
   │  ├─ SHA256:<fp> ✋ NO boot record match
   │  ├─ SHA256:<fp> ✔ matches the boot record
   └─ ✋ the boot record answered, and does NOT attest every offered key

  why: this endpoint offered a key the box's own record does not hold:
       SHA256:<fp>

       a host's public keys are public, so a real key beside a forged one
       is the cheap attack — every offered key is checked, never just one.
       ⇒ treat this as a security event, NOT as a stale record.
         the name 'grove-fixture-hetzner-1' may answer from a host that is not the box
  fix: confirm the tailnet names that box before you trust any key here —
    tailscale status | grep 'grove-fixture-hetzner-1'

## arm 2 · trust.gen, the pinned ssh fails
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-hetzner --mode apply --trust verified
   ├─ alias:    grove-fixture-hetzner
   ├─ endpoint: grove-fixture-hetzner-1:22
   ├─ tailnet:  no local tunnel — scan grove-fixture-hetzner-1 direct
   ├─ scanned:  2 key(s) offered
   └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: the ssh pinned to the trusted key (ssh-ed25519) did not answer (rc 255)

  why: that channel is what attests every other key, so no key was attested
  it said:
    Host key verification failed.
  fix: if it names a CHANGED host key or a failed verification, the trusted
       key itself no longer matches — a security event; confirm the box first:
    tailscale status | grep 'grove-fixture-hetzner-1'
  else wake the seat, then re-run —
    rhx git.grove.wake grove-fixture-hetzner

## arm 2 · trust.gen, the tailnet name offers no key
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-hetzner --mode plan --trust verified
   ├─ alias:    grove-fixture-hetzner
   ├─ endpoint: grove-fixture-hetzner-1:22
   ├─ tailnet:  no local tunnel — scan grove-fixture-hetzner-1 direct
   └─ 💥 grove-fixture-hetzner-1:22 offered no host keys in 1s

  why: the box did not answer at its tailnet name. either it is offline, this
       laptop is off the tailnet, or the box was replaced — a replacement
       joins under a NEW tailnet name, and the registry still names the old one
  fix: ask the tailnet which name is online —
    rhx network.tailnet.peers.get --match grove-fixture-hetzner
  a new name → adopt it (howto.adopt-a-replacement-grove); an offline one → wake it —
    rhx git.grove.wake grove-fixture-hetzner

