## arm 2 · trust.gen, a changed key
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-hetzner --mode apply --trust verified
   ├─ alias:    grove-fixture-hetzner
   ├─ endpoint: grove-fixture-hetzner-1:22
   ├─ tailnet:  no local tunnel — scan grove-fixture-hetzner-1 direct
   ├─ scanned:  2 key(s) offered
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: host key CHANGED for grove-fixture-hetzner-1 (ssh-ed25519)

  why: the tailnet name answered with a key other than the one on record —
       a REBUILT box, or a host that is not the box. a tailnet box has no
       console; the one attestation is the box's own report, over ssh
       pinned to a key still on record
  fix: confirm the tailnet names the box, then let a key still on record decide —
    tailscale status | grep 'grove-fixture-hetzner-1'
    rhx git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-hetzner --mode apply --on-changed replace
  if NO key on record still matches (a full rebuild), no channel here attests it:
  compare the fingerprints to infra's (its bootstrap prints them) before any write

