   ├─ tailnet:  no local tunnel — scan grove-fixture-hetzner-1 direct
   ├─ scanned:  2 key(s) offered
   ├─ changed:  ssh-ed25519 ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 (a replace is asked for; the boot record decides)
   ├─ 🌙 a REBUILT tailnet box — no key on record still matches, so no channel attests the change
   ├─ fingerprints
   │  ├─ SHA256:<fp> ✋ NO boot record match
   │  ├─ SHA256:<fp> ✋ NO boot record match
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: a rebuilt tailnet box, and no key on record still matches (ssh-ed25519 ecdsa-sha2-nistp256)

  why: no console, no boot record, and no trusted key left to pin ssh to —
       so no channel here attests the new keys, and none may be accepted on faith
  fix: compare the fingerprints above to infra's (its bootstrap prints them)
       before any write; a key that does not match is not the box

