## arm 2s · trust.gen, an ssm grove, a changed key
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-ec2 --mode apply --trust verified
   ├─ alias:    grove-fixture-ec2
   ├─ endpoint: localhost:<port>
   ├─ tunnel:   bound on ipv4 only (scan via 127.0.0.1)
   ├─ scanned:  2 key(s) offered
   ├─ labeled:  [localhost]:<port> (the name ssh looks up)
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: host key CHANGED for [localhost]:<port> (ssh-ed25519)

  why: this port previously answered with a different key. either the
       grove was rebuilt (or the port was reused by a NEW box), or
       another process now holds the local port
  fix: if the box is new, let this skill verify and replace the stale
       entry — it writes only when the box's OWN boot record confirms
       the key it just scanned —
    rhx git.grove.trust.gen --grove grove-fixture-ec2 --mode apply --on-changed replace
  and if THAT refuses, the boot record did not attest the scanned key —
  which is the second row above, so read what holds the port before you
  trust any key here —
    ss -tlnp | grep ':<port>'

